## CSS Architecture
- **Base**: Reset, typography, variables
- **Layout**: Grid, containers, spacing
- **Components**: Buttons, cards, forms, navigation
- **Utilities**: Animations, helpers, responsive

## Accessibility Standards
- **Color Contrast**: Minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text
- **Focus States**: Visible focus indicators on all interactive elements
- **Keyboard Navigation**: All interactive elements accessible via keyboard
- **Screen Readers**: Proper ARIA labels and semantic HTML
- **Touch Targets**: Minimum 44px for mobile interactions

## Performance Guidelines
- **CSS**: Use CSS custom properties for theming
- **Images**: Optimized formats (WebP with fallbacks)
- **Animations**: Use transform and opacity for GPU acceleration
- **Loading**: Lazy loading for images and non-critical content
- **Minification**: Compressed CSS in production

## Component Patterns

### Hero Section
- Full viewport height on mobile, 80vh on desktop
- Centered content with clear hierarchy
- Single call-to-action button
- Background with subtle animation

### Content Sections
- Consistent padding (2rem mobile, 4rem desktop)
- Grid layout for content/media
- Cards for feature highlights
- Smooth scroll animations

### Navigation
- Fixed header with backdrop blur
- Hamburger menu for mobile
- Smooth transitions for menu items
- Active state indicators

## Animation Classes
```scss
@keyframes fadeIn {
  from { opacity: 0; }
  to { opacity: 1; }
}

@keyframes slideUp {
  from { transform: translateY(30px); opacity: 0; }
  to { transform: translateY(0); opacity: 1; }
}

@keyframes scaleIn {
  from { transform: scale(0.9); opacity: 0; }
  to { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
}

.fade-in {
  animation: fadeIn 0.6s ease-out;
}

.slide-up {
  animation: slideUp 0.5s ease-out;
}

.scale-in {
  animation: scaleIn 0.4s ease-out;
}
```

